  "summary": "Malicious code in devplatform-nx-react (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package loads a bundled dropper (_support.js) that fingerprints the host OS and downloads a second-stage binary over HTTPS from three Cloudflare Workers mirrors (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at platform-specific paths (/pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS-TXT chunked fallback channel via *.dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe under TEMP on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c '... \u0026' on Unix).",
